---
description: Route net-new project ideas through the corporate/site harness
alwaysApply: true
---

For a net-new project idea, active corporate program, or site handoff, invoke the
matching corporate/site role instead of implementing immediately. Treat `program.json`
and current executable evidence as authoritative.

This Cursor Harness checkout is the factory that creates corporate folders — not
the product corporate root. Each program lives in its own corporate folder
(`--root`) that points at one site (`--site`). Never write `program.json` into
the site. Never use the site path as the corporate root. Never nest `--root`
under `--site` (including factory `programs/<id>`). Keep corporate and site
phases in separate Cursor workspaces. Never call `move_agent_to_root` across
corporate and site. If the active root is the wrong plane, stop and ask the
user to open the other folder; do not continue from the wrong root.

Product sites must not edit factory sources (`src/corp_harness/**`) or factory
plugin sources. Portfolio CLI (`corp-harness portfolio`) is factory platform code,
not a product-site deliverable. Factory product features require
`corp-harness init --kind factory` and a user-recorded `factory_authorization`
artifact before corporate acceptance. Agents never pass `--actor user`, never
infer a passed gate, expose secrets, or grant user approval.

Ordinary scoped coding work outside a harness program is unaffected.
See `premium-model-policy` for Sol/Fable routing.
